== News and Awards
- Tyler received the International Neural Network Society's 2025 Aharon Katzir Young Investigator Award, presented at the 2026 IEEE World Congress on Computational Intelligence
- Tyler was recognized among the 2025 World's Top 2% Scientists by Stanford/Elsevier, with research supported through this NSF award contributing to the broader research portfolio underlying the recognition
- Our survey ``Towards Trustworthy Retrieval Augmented Generation for Large Language Models: A Survey'' was published in ACM Computing Surveys
- Our paper ``Risk-Controlled Event-Driven Cascading Updates for Knowledge Graph Consistency Restoration'' was published in Findings of ACL 2026, introducing the ICEWS14-Event and YAGO-Event benchmark datasets for evolving knowledge graphs
- Our paper ``Ensemble Privacy Defense for Knowledge-Intensive LLMs against Membership Inference Attacks'' was published in Findings of EACL 2026
- Our survey ``A Survey on LLM-based Conversational User Simulation'' was published at EACL 2026
- We released two new preprints on graph-based sparse personalization and multi-trajectory reasoning for personalized generation
- GraphRAG and personalized LLM research from the project is being incorporated into Tyler's Social Network Analysis course at Vanderbilt
- Vanderbilt established the new College of Connected Computing, creating new opportunities for the project's graph learning, RAG, and generative AI research to contribute to emerging programs including the MS in AI
- Tyler is awarded the NSF III Small Award ``Towards Well-Rounded Graph Retrieval for Retrieval-Augmented Generation''!

